-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Video moderation gets a voice — THE ENUM VALUES ONLY.
--
-- GENERATED BY `pnpm db:generate`, which works again since the `0146` baseline. The header is
-- hand-written because the tool records WHAT changed and never WHY.
--
-- ## `redirected_to_source`
--
-- A third disposition, and the one that makes copyright reporting honest on a platform that hosts
-- no bytes. `report_dismissed` says "we looked, the claim does not hold". For a YouTube-hosted
-- video a rights-holder's real remedy is a YouTube claim — hiding the row here withdraws Qatoto's
-- copy while the video keeps playing on youtube.com — so filing that answer as a dismissal tells
-- somebody they were wrong when the truth is they asked the wrong platform.
--
-- It touches no content: the report closes, `moderation_visibility_state` is untouched, the video
-- still serves. The report's `status` stays `dismissed`, because no content action was taken and a
-- fourth status would ripple through `video_content_report_resolution_ck` and every queue filter
-- for nothing. The ACTION KIND carries the meaning.
--
-- ## The two notification kinds
--
-- Video moderation notified NOBODY. The enum already carried §10 kinds added with the comment
-- "the submitter has no way to learn the answer except by re-checking the page" — which described
-- video reports exactly.
--
-- `video_report_decided` -> the REPORTER, on every close.
-- `video_content_actioned` -> the CREATOR, and ONLY when their content actually moved.
--
-- ⚠️ A CREATOR IS DELIBERATELY NOT TOLD ABOUT A DISMISSED OR REDIRECTED REPORT. Nothing happened
-- to their video, and "you were reported and we let it go" hands them a grievance plus a very
-- small suspect pool — the retaliation risk that already keeps reporter identity hidden from
-- moderators.
--
-- ## WHY THIS FILE IS ENUM VALUES AND NOTHING ELSE
--
-- Postgres refuses `ALTER TYPE ... ADD VALUE` in a transaction that later USES the value, and
-- drizzle runs each file as one transaction — the reason `0128`/`0129` split. Nothing here needs a
-- table change: `video_content_report.resolution_note` ALREADY EXISTS. It was added long ago,
-- undocumented, and **nothing has ever written or read it** — the same "column with no writer"
-- shape as `video_collaborator.status` before the accept route. This change is what finally uses it.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

ALTER TYPE "public"."video_moderation_action_kind" ADD VALUE 'redirected_to_source';--> statement-breakpoint
ALTER TYPE "public"."notification_kind" ADD VALUE 'video_report_decided' BEFORE 'platform_role_change_proposed';--> statement-breakpoint
ALTER TYPE "public"."notification_kind" ADD VALUE 'video_content_actioned' BEFORE 'platform_role_change_proposed';
